Dead code is gone: `codebrain` in the braindecode backend, which had no registry entry; the `FoundationModelSpec` fields `pretrained_ch_names`, `supports_channel_interpolation` and `fallback_backends`, which nothing read (the documentation's foundation-model table loses its "Interpolation" column, always "no"); and the extraction metadata `original_sfreq` and `channel_mapping`, which repeated `input_sfreq` and `original_channels` with `model_channels` and were never written to embedding files. The in-memory frozen-backbone embedding cache keeps one backbone's embeddings at a time instead of growing with every backbone a process runs; the documentation called it a disk cache.
